WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.062 --> 00:00:07.053
For days the Hwalbindang trained with spears and swords.

2
00:00:07.054 --> 00:00:13.378
Gildong taught them everything he had read about weapons and fighting.

3
00:00:13.379 --> 00:00:16.819
"Robbing the temple was easy," Gildong said.

4
00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:22.836
"Robbing a government storehouse will be much more dangerous."

5
00:00:22.837 --> 00:00:28.899
When he thought they were ready, they went to Hamheung.

6
00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:34.649
Outside the city some of the Hwalbindang gathered straw.

7
00:00:34.650 --> 00:00:38.982
Late that night they went to the old royal villa.

8
00:00:38.983 --> 00:00:43.674
They piled the straw outside the walls. Gildong

9
00:00:43.675 --> 00:00:49.729
took out his fan. "Fire!" Thwoosh!

10
00:00:49.730 --> 00:00:58.831
The straw lit up in a bright blaze. ***

11
00:00:58.832 --> 00:01:03.123
The governor in Hamheung was eating a late dinner.

12
00:01:03.124 --> 00:01:07.629
Outside, he heard the city bells ringing.

13
00:01:07.630 --> 00:01:13.733
He sighed. "I hope it's nothing important."

14
00:01:13.734 --> 00:01:18.394
Just then the captain of the city soldiers arrived.

15
00:01:18.395 --> 00:01:23.970
"Why are you interrupting my meal?" the governor snapped.

16
00:01:23.971 --> 00:01:28.603
"Sir, there's a fire at the royal villa," the captain said.

17
00:01:28.604 --> 00:01:35.991
"What?" The governor ran outside.

18
00:01:35.992 --> 00:01:40.080
He saw flames in the distance.

19
00:01:40.081 --> 00:01:42.658
"Quick! We must put out the fire!"

20
00:01:42.659 --> 00:01:46.273
"I already sent some soldiers," the captain said.

21
00:01:46.274 --> 00:01:50.004
"Some soldiers?" the governor cried.

22
00:01:50.005 --> 00:01:51.589
"It's the royal villa!

23
00:01:51.590 --> 00:01:54.087
Send every soldier in the city.

24
00:01:54.088 --> 00:01:58.004
Wake the townspeople too!"

25
00:01:58.005 --> 00:02:06.349
*** The Hwalbindang were waiting near the government

26
00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:10.255
office. Gildong watched as soldiers ran out the

27
00:02:10.256 --> 00:02:12.146
gate. "Just as I thought!

28
00:02:12.147 --> 00:02:16.779
All the soldiers are leaving to put out the fire," he said.

29
00:02:16.780 --> 00:02:22.500
"No one's guarding the storehouse. Let's go!"

30
00:02:22.501 --> 00:02:27.888
The thieves made their way into the government office.

31
00:02:27.889 --> 00:02:34.242
They loaded grain and valuables from the storehouse onto carts.

32
00:02:34.243 --> 00:02:42.218
"There's so much here!" Mok said.

33
00:02:42.219 --> 00:02:47.328
When they finished, Gildong put a sign on the gate.

34
00:02:47.329 --> 00:02:50.474
"What does that say?" Chibong asked.

35
00:02:50.475 --> 00:02:54.672
"'The Hwalbindang were here,'" Gildong said.

36
00:02:54.673 --> 00:02:57.433
"'This is your punishment for unfair taxes.

37
00:02:57.434 --> 00:03:14.255
Don't mistreat the people again!'"

38
00:03:14.256 --> 00:03:19.948
*** Lord Hong listened as Police Chief Heup reported to the

39
00:03:19.949 --> 00:03:25.265
king. "Someone started a fire at the royal villa?" the king

40
00:03:25.266 --> 00:03:31.849
cried. "The government office was robbed too? Who's

41
00:03:31.850 --> 00:03:36.028
responsible?" "These bandits are the same ones who robbed the temple in

42
00:03:36.029 --> 00:03:38.835
Hapcheon. They call themselves the

43
00:03:38.836 --> 00:03:45.346
Hwalbindang. People say their leader is a boy—Hong Gildong.

44
00:03:45.347 --> 00:03:50.913
He gives the stolen grain to the poor."

45
00:03:50.914 --> 00:03:56.804
"A boy is causing all this trouble?" the king cried.

46
00:03:56.805 --> 00:04:04.164
Lord Hong gasped. "It can't be," he thought.

47
00:04:04.165 --> 00:04:09.500
"Are you all right, minister?" the king asked.

48
00:04:09.501 --> 00:04:12.316
"I apologize, Your Majesty.

49
00:04:12.317 --> 00:04:16.473
I'm suddenly feeling unwell," Lord Hong said.

50
00:04:16.474 --> 00:04:18.628
"Please excuse me."

51
00:04:18.629 --> 00:04:23.413
Lord Hong bowed.

52
00:04:23.414 --> 00:04:27.519
As he left, he heard the king's command.

53
00:04:27.520 --> 00:04:35.930
"Chief Heup, capture Hong Gildong!"

